# THIS IS THE FILE THAT GOVERNS EVERY COMPOSE BUILD.
#
# Both Dockerfiles take the repo root as their build context (they need
# pnpm-lock.yaml and pnpm-workspace.yaml), and Docker reads the .dockerignore
# beside the *context*, never one inside a subdirectory. apps/api/.dockerignore
# and apps/web/.dockerignore mirror these rules for anyone building an app on
# its own, but they are not what `docker compose build` consults -- if you add
# an exclusion, add it here.

# Installed inside the image from the lockfile. Copying the host's tree in would
# be slower, larger, and wrong: pnpm's store is full of absolute symlinks that
# point at paths which don't exist in the container.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Regenerated in the build stage; a stale copy from the host is
# how you end up debugging code that isn't in the image.
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
out
**/out
build
**/build
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. Everything the containers need arrives through env_file and
# `environment:` at run time -- baking a .env into an image freezes it into the
# layer history. .env.example is documentation and harmless, but there is no
# reason for the build to see it either.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Generated invoice PDFs. They carry customer names, numbers and amounts, and
# the container keeps them on a named volume instead.
apps/api/uploads

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Editor, agent and tooling scratch.
.claude
.vscode
.idea
.playwright-mcp
.DS_Store

# Not inputs to a build.
README.md
DEPLOY.md
CLAUDE.md
design-reference
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.override.yml
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
**/.dockerignore
